Recommends: wmctrl
Description: System-tray launcher for scrcpy (KDE/Plasma friendly)
 scrcpy-tray puts a persistent icon in the system tray from which you can
 launch scrcpy for any connected Android device, apply presets (fullscreen,
 no-audio, size, bitrate, recording…), connect over Wi-Fi and stop mirroring.
 .
 It is built on Qt's QSystemTrayIcon, which uses the StatusNotifierItem D-Bus
 protocol, so it integrates natively with KDE Plasma on both X11 and Wayland.
 Connected devices are detected in real time via the adb track-devices stream.
